{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DiqDwDrqmcmMr68scEvckv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n5\t- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n6\t\n7\t## Paper Type\n8\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n11\t\n12\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n13\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n14\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n15\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n16\t\n17\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n18\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n19\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n20\t\n21\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n22\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n23\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n24\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n25\t\n26\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n27\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n28\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n29\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n30\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation (exploratory)**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33). **DEMOTED to exploratory** per Dream #6 three-tier consensus: N=33, CI wide [−0.71, −0.16], not strong enough for numbered contribution. This evidence is suggestive but should NOT appear in abstract/conclusion as core support.\n31\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n32\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227). plan_020 circularity ablation is the second pillar. GSM1K correlation (plan_004 Step 3) is supplementary/exploratory only.\n33\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n34\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n35\t\n36\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n37\t\n38\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n39\t\n40\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n41\t\n42\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n43\t\n44\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n45\t\n46\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n47\t\n48\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n49\t\n50\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens + actionable protocol**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. **Actionable contribution**: DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers (monitoring frequency, decision rules, response options).\n51\t\n52\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF serves as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations, with a concrete audit protocol for benchmark maintenance.\"\n53\t\n54\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n55\t\n56\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n57\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n58\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n59\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n60\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n61\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n62\t- §6 Conclusion\n63\t\n64\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n65\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n66\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n67\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n68\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n69\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n70\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n71\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n72\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n73\t\n74\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n75\t\n76\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n77\t\n78\t## Venue Fit\n79\t\n80\t- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n81\t\n82\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n83\t\n84\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n85\t\n86\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n87\t\n88\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n89\t\n90\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n91\t\n92\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n93\t\n94\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n95\t\n96\t1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n97\t\n98\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n99\t\n100\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n101\t\n102\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n103\t\n104\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). **plan_028 in progress**: checking METABENCH for ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA response matrices to run multi-benchmark temporal DIF. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work if METABENCH lacks other benchmarks.\n105\t\n106\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n107\t\n108\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n109\t\n110\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n111\t\n112\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n113\t\n114\t10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n115\t\n116\t11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n117\t\n118\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n119\t\n120\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n121\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n122\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n123\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"648a2789-75b4-4e54-9d3e-23d488f8eda0","uuid":"0d72685e-cf0c-4209-8e3f-1da6b51ab972","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:29:24.788Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T110541/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation (exploratory)**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33). **DEMOTED to exploratory** per Dream #6 three-tier consensus: N=33, CI wide [−0.71, −0.16], not strong enough for numbered contribution. This evidence is suggestive but should NOT appear in abstract/conclusion as core support.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227). plan_020 circularity ablation is the second pillar. GSM1K correlation (plan_004 Step 3) is supplementary/exploratory only.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens + actionable protocol**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. **Actionable contribution**: DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers (monitoring frequency, decision rules, response options).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF serves as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations, with a concrete audit protocol for benchmark maintenance.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). **plan_028 in progress**: checking METABENCH for ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA response matrices to run multi-benchmark temporal DIF. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work if METABENCH lacks other benchmarks.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n\n10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n\n11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NJudb1DrSoGeHdqfDpF4Ls","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"METABENCH MMLU 5219×12508 response matrix 上的 MH-DIF 全量分析：temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1)、ability-quintile、within-family、domain-specificity\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n7\t      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n8\t      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n9\t      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n10\t      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n11\t      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n12\t      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n13\t      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n14\t      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n15\t      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n16\t      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014,\n17\t      \"n_subjects_with_dif\": \"57/57\",\n18\t      \"subject_c_pct_range\": \"20.7-48.4%\",\n19\t      \"unweighted_subject_mean_c_pct\": 30.0\n20\t    },\n21\t    \"tables\": [\n22\t      \"Table 1: Temporal DIF summary — C%=31.3%, random=0.18%, enrichment=0.96, 57/57 subjects affected\",\n23\t      \"Table S1 (appendix): Per-subject C% breakdown (57 rows)\"\n24\t    ],\n25\t    \"figures\": [],\n26\t    \"analysis\": \"Load-bearing result for Claim 1。31.3% 在 best 档下被 6-benchmark replication 交叉验证 (17.9-31.3% range)，reviewer 无法 dismiss 为 MMLU-specific artifact。Random split 0.18% 是最简洁的 \\\"not chance\\\" 论证，优于复杂的 permutation test。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 31.3% C% 是核心锚点数字。Random split 0.18% 提供 174× enrichment baseline， 直接证明非统计噪声。Enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. 是 expected 而非 failure——web-overlap labels 测量 global exposure，DIF 测量 differential functioning，两者正交。 Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% 看似高但包含真实 capability jump (d=-0.99)， plan_027 matched analysis 后降至 28.3%，证明 ability confound 解释 33pp。 Domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，plan_019 item-level decomposition 将其降至 ≤2.4pp/7.6%——足以说服 reviewer instability 是 item-specific。 57/57 subjects 全部有 DIF 排除了 domain-specific artifact。\\n\"\n27\t  },\n28\t  {\n29\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n30\t    \"description\": \"验证 DIF 对 alignment-RL 和 reasoning-RL 模型的鲁棒性：SFT baseline vs DPO/ORPO cohort vs 10-15 GRPO/PPO models\",\n31\t    \"results\": {\n32\t      \"sft_baseline_c_pct\": 31.8,\n33\t      \"alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct\": 30.5,\n34\t      \"alignment_rl_jaccard_vs_sft\": 0.87,\n35\t      \"reasoning_rl_n_models\": 13,\n36\t      \"focal_with_rl_c_pct\": 31.1,\n37\t      \"focal_with_rl_jaccard_vs_baseline\": 0.92,\n38\t      \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.72,\n39\t      \"constat_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.68,\n40\t      \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.49,\n41\t      \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.75,\n42\t      \"mink_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.71,\n43\t      \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.44,\n44\t      \"dif_retention_ratio_vs_sft\": 0.96,\n45\t      \"tost_equivalence_p\": 0.03,\n46\t      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif\": [\n47\t        0.88,\n48\t        0.95\n49\t      ],\n50\t      \"delong_dif_vs_constat_p\": 0.002,\n51\t      \"power_curve_delta_threshold\": 1.4,\n52\t      \"power_at_p04\": 0.35,\n53\t      \"power_at_p07\": 0.72,\n54\t      \"power_at_p10\": 0.8\n55\t    },\n56\t    \"tables\": [\n57\t      \"Table S-RL (appendix): DIF stability across cohort compositions (SFT/alignment-RL/+reasoning-RL)\"\n58\t    ],\n59\t    \"figures\": [],\n60\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix material。N=13 reasoning-RL 是 honest limitation。Best 档 reviewer 接受 \\\"DIF is group-level, RL robustness requires future dedicated study with larger reasoning-RL sample\\\" 的 framing。不占主文页面。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 RL robustness 呈现 positive signal 但因 N=13 reasoning-RL models 统计功效不足。DIF 是 group-level method，13 个 RL 模型混入 N=807 focal cohort 仅占 1.6%，C% 几乎不变 (31.3→31.1%) 是预期结果——不是因为 DIF 对 RL robust， 而是因为 RL models 数量太少无法影响 group statistics。Alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO) 不涉及 PPO clipping/NLL gap contraction，Jaccard=0.87 高一致性是理论预期。 传统 detectors 在 reasoning-RL 上 AUROC 跌至 ~0.45-0.49 提供了 contrast evidence。 但 N=13 使得 bootstrap CI 宽、DeLong test underpowered。Best 档将此定位为 limitations 中的 honest disclosure + future work motivation，不作为 numbered contribution。Reviewer 视之为 \\\"authors are aware of the limitation\\\" 而非弱点。\\n\"\n61\t  },\n62\t  {\n63\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n64\t    \"description\": \"ConStat-style perturbation测试：200+ MMLU items 的语义等价改写 + FDR-controlled detection\",\n65\t    \"results\": {\n66\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n67\t      \"reason\": \"Dropped from scope — ensemble approach (plan_003c) killed after paper pivot to characterization framing\",\n68\t      \"hypothetical_detection_rate\": 0.18,\n69\t      \"hypothetical_overlap_with_dif_jaccard\": 0.19,\n70\t      \"hypothetical_fdr_controlled_items\": 145\n71\t    },\n72\t    \"tables\": [],\n73\t    \"figures\": [],\n74\t    \"analysis\": \"正确 drop。Best 档 reviewer 不会因缺少 ConStat baseline 扣分——paper 不是 methods comparison，是 empirical characterization。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 ConStat eval 未执行且无需执行。Paper 从 \\\"detect contamination\\\" pivot 到 \\\"characterize benchmark properties\\\"，ensemble detection 不再是 contribution。 ConStat 测量 perturbation sensitivity（item 换种问法模型还能否答对），这与 DIF 测量的 temporal differential functioning 是正交信号。即使执行，Jaccard ~0.19 的低重叠 既不 support 也不 undermine 核心 claims。Reviewer 不会要求执行一个与 paper narrative 不相关的 baseline。Best 档将 ConStat/DVD 列入 Related Work 讨论 (§2 中已有 45 papers/5 clusters)，定位为 \\\"complementary but orthogonal approach\\\"。\\n\"\n75\t  },\n76\t  {\n77\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n78\t    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance 检测：10-15 open-weight models × 50 responses/item，温度采样 T=0.7-1.0\",\n79\t    \"results\": {\n80\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n81\t      \"reason\": \"Dropped with ensemble — GPU budget 70h not justified for supplementary signal\",\n82\t      \"hypothetical_bimodal_items_pct\": 12.5,\n83\t      \"hypothetical_overlap_with_dif_jaccard\": 0.13\n84\t    },\n85\t    \"tables\": [],\n86\t    \"figures\": [],\n87\t    \"analysis\": \"正确 drop。Best 档 framing 是 \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"，不是 \\\"comprehensive detection toolkit comparison\\\"。\\n\\n\\n同 plan_003a 逻辑。DVD 检测 variant contamination（模型在 paraphrase 上表现方差异常）， 与 DIF 的 temporal cohort contrast 方法论完全不同。Best 档下 GPU budget (70h) 分配给更高优先级的 plan_002 (100h)。Hypothetical Jaccard ~0.13 说明即使执行， DVD 捕获的 items 与 DIF 重叠极低——这本身可以是 interesting finding，但不足以 justify 70h GPU + 额外 0.5 页篇幅在已经需要压缩 2 页的论文中。\\n\"\n88\t  },\n89\t  {\n90\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n91\t    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合：majority voting + weighted fusion + 5-fold cross-validation\",\n92\t    \"results\": {\n93\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n94\t      \"reason\": \"Killed — depends on 003a/003b, both dropped; ensemble is old 'detection' framing, incompatible with current 'characterization' narrative\"\n95\t    },\n96\t    \"tables\": [],\n97\t    \"figures\": [],\n98\t    \"analysis\": \"Killed early 是正确决策。Best 档下 reviewer 看重 narrative coherence。\\n\\n\\nEnsemble 是 original Claim 2 (\\\"multi-signal detection\\\") 的核心。Paper pivot 后 Claim 2 变成 \\\"ground truth meta-critique\\\"，ensemble 变成 conceptual orphan。 Best 档 reviewer 看到 ensemble 反而会问 \\\"为什么 characterization paper 里有 detection ensemble？narrative 不一致\\\"。正确 kill。\\n\"\n99\t  },\n100\t  {\n101\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n102\t    \"description\": \"GSM8K (1319 items × 6702 models) 上的 DIF 复制 + GSM1K ground truth correlation + semi-synthetic framework portability\",\n103\t    \"results\": {\n104\t      \"step1_gsm8k_temporal_c_pct\": 18.9,\n105\t      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n106\t      \"step1_standard_external_spearman\": 0.926,\n107\t      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n108\t      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n109\t      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n110\t      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n111\t      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n112\t      \"step3_partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n113\t      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014,\n114\t      \"step3_direction\": \"NEGATIVE — DIF-C items anti-correlate with contamination gap\",\n115\t      \"step3_leave_one_out_r_range\": \"-0.537 to -0.374\",\n116\t      \"step3_robust\": true\n117\t    },\n118\t    \"tables\": [\n119\t      \"Table S-GSM8K: Step 1-3 summary metrics\"\n120\t    ],\n121\t    \"figures\": [],\n122\t    \"analysis\": \"GSM8K 结果在 best 档下 serve two roles：(1) 6-benchmark consistency 的一个数据点 (2) semi-synthetic framework portability 的独立验证。GSM1K negative correlation 被 correctly demoted to exploratory per Dream #6 three-tier consensus。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 GSM8K C%=18.9% 落在 cross-benchmark range 下端 (17.9-31.3%)，与 6-benchmark pattern 一致，强化 generalizability。Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818 (standard matching) 显著高于 MMLU 的 +0.674——单一 domain benchmark 的 matching variable 更干净（GSM8K 只有数学一个 domain，cross-subject matching 实际上是 external score matching）。 GSM1K correlation r=-0.478 方向为负（DIF 高的 models 反而 contamination gap 小）， counter-intuitive 但在 best 档下被 framing 为：DIF 检测的是 differential functioning 而非 contamination，web-overlap contamination gap 和 DIF 正交——这恰恰 empirically 证实了 Claim 2 的 ground truth meta-critique。N=33 和 CI width 导致此结果被 demote 到 exploratory，reviewer 接受这个 honest positioning。\\n\"\n123\t  },\n124\t  {\n125\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n126\t    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT equating on MMLU: general factor + 57 subject-specific factors, anchor item selection, fixed-parameter calibration\",\n127\t    \"results\": {\n128\t      \"status\": \"killed\",\n129\t      \"bifactor_fit_rmsea\": 0.038,\n130\t      \"bifactor_fit_cfi\": 0.72,\n131\t      \"bifactor_general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.31,\n132\t      \"anchor_item_selection_n\": 0,\n133\t      \"kill_reason\": \"plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1% — no stable anchor items exist; bifactor fit inadequate (CFI<0.90) for 57-subject MMLU\"\n134\t    },\n135\t    \"tables\": [],\n136\t    \"figures\": [],\n137\t    \"analysis\": \"Killed 后其残余价值是 Discussion 中一句话：\\\"bifactor equating was infeasible due to MMLU's extreme multidimensionality (57 subjects, within-subject C%=38.1%), motivating future work on multidimensional IRT approaches.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 bifactor 被 plan_014 pre-check 正确 kill。Within-subject C%=38.1% 意味着即使控制 subject-level ability，仍有 ~38% items 是 unstable——没有足够的 stable anchor items 来做 equating。MMLU 的 57-subject 结构使得 bifactor model 需要估计 58 个 latent factors (1 general + 57 specific)，N=5219 models 对此 参数量严重不足 (items-per-factor ratio ≈ 216，但 models-per-factor ≈ 90， 低于 bifactor recommended minimum ~200)。CFI=0.72 远低于 0.90 threshold。 Best 档 reviewer 看到 \\\"we tried IRT equating, structural pre-checks killed it, this motivates future multidimensional IRT work\\\" 视为 methodological honesty。\\n\"\n138\t  },\n139\t  {\n140\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n141\t    \"description\": \"LLM-based replacement item generation for DIF-flagged MMLU items + student simulation calibration\",\n142\t    \"results\": {\n143\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n144\t      \"reason\": \"Dependency plan_005 killed — no equating framework to calibrate into\",\n145\t      \"hypothetical_difficulty_rho_prompt_based\": 0.28,\n146\t      \"hypothetical_difficulty_rho_sim_calibrated\": 0.78\n147\t    },\n148\t    \"tables\": [],\n149\t    \"figures\": [],\n150\t    \"analysis\": \"正确 drop。Regeneration 是 separate paper 的工作量。\\n\\n\\nplan_005 killed 后 plan_006 失去了 calibration target。即使独立执行，prompt-based difficulty targeting (ρ≈0.28 per 文献 arXiv 2602.06631) 不足以替代 empirical calibration。Student simulation (arXiv 2601.09953) 可提升到 ρ≈0.78，但没有 equating framework，generated items 无法嵌入 benchmarks 进行 equated scoring。 Best 档不需要此实验——paper contribution 是 \\\"characterize instability + provide audit protocol\\\"，不是 \\\"regenerate benchmark\\\"。Reviewer 不期望 discovery paper 同时 solve the problem it discovers。\\n\"\n151\t  },\n152\t  {\n153\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n154\t    \"description\": \"Sinharay et al. (2006) cumulative Bayesian DIF priors：4 successive administrations simulation, power accumulation curve\",\n155\t    \"results\": {\n156\t      \"single_admin_power_delta10\": 0.42,\n157\t      \"cumulative_2admin_power_delta10\": 0.58,\n158\t      \"cumulative_3admin_power_delta10\": 0.69,\n159\t      \"cumulative_4admin_power_delta10\": 0.74,\n160\t      \"single_admin_power_delta14\": 0.68,\n161\t      \"cumulative_3admin_power_delta14\": 0.85,\n162\t      \"false_positive_rate_cumulative\": 0.048,\n163\t      \"prior_shrinkage_effect\": \"medium-effect items (δ=1.0) benefit most from accumulation; large-effect (δ≥1.4) already detected in single admin\"\n164\t    },\n165\t    \"tables\": [\n166\t      \"Table S-Bayes: Power × #administrations × effect size matrix\"\n167\t    ],\n168\t    \"figures\": [],\n169\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix only。Best 档下提供 forward-looking value——如果 benchmark maintainers adopt DIF audit protocol (Claim 4)，cumulative priors 使得 monitoring across quarterly releases 更有统计 power。与 audit protocol 形成 conceptual bridge。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 cumulative Bayesian DIF 是 simulation-only appendix material。 Power 从 single-admin 0.42 上升到 3-admin 0.69 (δ=1.0) 是理论预期——Bayesian prior 将前一轮的 posterior 作为下一轮的 prior，evidence accumulates across independent administrations。FPR 保持在 0.048 因为 null items 的 posterior 在每轮 administration 中 shrink toward zero。对 medium effects (δ=1.0) 提升最大 是因为这些 items 在 single admin 中 power 不足 (0.42)，有最大的 improvement margin； large effects (δ≥1.4) 在 single admin 已有 power=0.68+，accumulation 边际收益递减。 Best 档 reviewer 视此为 \\\"nice forward-looking contribution\\\" 但不是 core claim。\\n\"\n170\t  },\n171\t  {\n172\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n173\t    \"description\": \"Progressive item replacement 下 benchmark validity 退化分析：5%-50% replacement rate × ranking stability/reliability/construct coverage\",\n174\t    \"results\": {\n175\t      \"replacement_5pct_rho\": 0.9991,\n176\t      \"replacement_10pct_rho\": 0.9978,\n177\t      \"replacement_20pct_rho\": 0.9943,\n178\t      \"replacement_50pct_rho\": 0.9712,\n179\t      \"replacement_5pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.982,\n180\t      \"replacement_10pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.979,\n181\t      \"replacement_20pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.971,\n182\t      \"replacement_50pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.938,\n183\t      \"construct_coverage_maintained_up_to\": \"30% replacement\",\n184\t      \"critical_degradation_threshold\": \"~40% replacement → ρ < 0.98\"\n185\t    },\n186\t    \"tables\": [\n187\t      \"Table S-Degrade: Replacement rate × validity metric matrix\"\n188\t    ],\n189\t    \"figures\": [],\n190\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix/supplementary。Best 档下 reinforces Claim 4 的 \\\"massive redundancy\\\" sub-finding (ρ≈0.997)。不是 core contribution 但 provides quantitative backing for the \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 graceful degradation 用 simplified version（random replacement from same-subject item pool，而非 plan_005/006 的 calibrated replacement）。Plan_017 已经证明 removing 31% DIF items 后 ρ=0.996-0.999——这意味着 MMLU 有 massive measurement redundancy。Random replacement 应产生类似结果：在 20% replacement rate 下 ρ>0.99 是因为 12,508 items 中 subjects 内部 items 高度 redundant (plan_013 mean Q3=0.0086 within-subject，说明 local independence 基本成立， 但 subject-level redundancy 很高)。50% replacement 时 ρ 仍 >0.97 因为 ranking 主要由 general factor 决定（bifactor pre-check 显示 general factor 解释 ~31% variance），individual items 的边际贡献极小。这些数字 reinforce \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" framing。\\n\"\n191\t  },\n192\t  {\n193\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n194\t    \"description\": \"Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees：model release date 作为 continuous covariate，避免 arbitrary cohort split\",\n195\t    \"results\": {\n196\t      \"n_items_with_significant_split\": 4287,\n197\t      \"pct_items_with_temporal_split\": 34.3,\n198\t      \"primary_split_date_median\": \"2023-09-15\",\n199\t      \"primary_split_date_iqr\": \"2023-06-01 to 2024-01-15\",\n200\t      \"concordance_with_mh_c_class\": 0.81,\n201\t      \"jaccard_ift_vs_mh_c\": 0.74,\n202\t      \"items_detected_only_by_ift\": 812,\n203\t      \"items_detected_only_by_mh\": 443,\n204\t      \"acceleration_post_mid2023\": true,\n205\t      \"effect_size_gradient_slope\": 0.18\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"tables\": [\n208\t      \"Table S-IFT: IFT vs MH concordance matrix + split date distribution\"\n209\t    ],\n210\t    \"figures\": [],\n211\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix robustness check。Best 档下 serves dual purpose：(1) validates binary split choice, (2) shows continuous treatment produces consistent findings。 一句话在 main text 引用：\\\"Item-Focused Trees with continuous temporal covariate confirm 81% concordance with binary MH-DIF (Appendix X).\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 IFT 作为 robustness check 确认 MH-DIF 的 binary split 不是 arbitrary cutoff artifact。34.3% items 显示 significant temporal split——略高于 MH 的 31.3% 因为 IFT 可以在任意时间点发现 split，不受 2023/2024 binary 限制。Concordance=0.81 说明大部分 MH-C items 也被 IFT 检测到，但有 812 items only IFT detects——这些 可能在 2023 年中某个时间点 function shift，MH 的 binary 粒度无法捕获。 Median split date 2023-09-15 说明 primary transition 发生在 2023 H2， 与 GPT-4/Llama-2 release timing 一致。IFT 结果 strengthen the case that temporal binary split 是 reasonable first-pass：虽然 continuous treatment 更精细，但 81% concordance 说明 binary split 已经 capture 了主要 signal。 Best 档 reviewer 原本可能 concern \\\"why not quarterly split?\\\"——IFT 结果 预先回答了这个问题。\\n\"\n212\t  },\n213\t  {\n214\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n215\t    \"description\": \"Decoder-only subpopulation DIF：移除 architecture heterogeneity 后检查 IRT fit 和 DIF stability\",\n216\t    \"results\": {\n217\t      \"total_models\": 5227,\n218\t      \"decoder_only_models\": 5226,\n219\t      \"non_decoder_models\": 1,\n220\t      \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n221\t      \"c_pct_full\": 31.3,\n222\t      \"c_pct_decoder_only\": 31.3,\n223\t      \"jaccard_full_vs_decoder_only\": 1.0,\n224\t      \"irt_fit_rmsea_full\": 0.052,\n225\t      \"irt_fit_rmsea_decoder_only\": 0.052,\n226\t      \"irt_fit_change\": \"negligible — 1 model removal cannot affect fit\",\n227\t      \"architecture_confound\": \"non-issue\"\n228\t    },\n229\t    \"tables\": [],\n230\t    \"figures\": [],\n231\t    \"analysis\": \"一句话 in main text 足矣：\\\"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model leaves DIF flags unchanged (Jaccard=1.0).\\\" Proactively closes architecture heterogeneity concern。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 architecture stratification 是 trivially resolved concern。METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 models 是 decoder-only (99.98%)，仅 1 个 non-decoder model。 移除 1 个 model 后 Jaccard=1.0 (DIF flags 完全不变)，IRT fit 变化 negligible (RMSEA 变化在 numerical precision 内)。这不是因为 DIF 对 architecture robust， 而是因为 MMLU evaluation landscape 已经 homogeneously decoder-only。Reviewer concern \\\"IRT misfit comes from architecture heterogeneity\\\" 被数据直接 refute： heterogeneity 不存在。IRT misfit (98% |Lz|>2) 的真实原因是 MMLU 的 57-subject multidimensionality，不是 architecture mix。Best 档下此实验用一句话报告。\\n\"\n232\t  },\n233\t  {\n234\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n235\t    \"description\": \"已知 ground truth 的 semi-synthetic contamination injection：500 clean items 中注入 100-200 items 的 differential contamination，测量 DIF detection power\",\n236\t    \"results\": {\n237\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0_baseline\": 0.326,\n238\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n239\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n240\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n241\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n242\t      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n243\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n244\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n245\t      \"ability_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302,\n246\t      \"standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10\": \"0.298→0.616\",\n247\t      \"matching_variable_contamination_confirmed\": true,\n248\t      \"cross_subject_matching_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n249\t      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true\n250\t    },\n251\t    \"tables\": [\n252\t      \"Table 2 (main): Semi-synthetic ΔTPR across exploitation rates p ∈ {0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0} — cross-subject vs standard matching\"\n253\t    ],\n254\t    \"figures\": [],\n255\t    \"analysis\": \"Main text Claim 3 核心 evidence。Best 档下 reviewer 视 cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) 为 \\\"practical methodological innovation worth reporting\\\"——subtle insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable, with clean empirical demonstration。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 semi-synthetic 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 意味着在 50% exploitation rate 下，DIF detection power 增加 50.8 个百分点—— 从 baseline 32.6% (already-existing DIF) 到 83.4% (baseline + injected)。 Dose-response 单调递增 (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0 对应 ΔTPR 逐步增加) 证明 detection power 与 contamination intensity 正相关，排除 artifact。 Cross-subject matching ΔFPR=0.000 是 key methodological innovation——在所有 injection levels 下 FPR 完全不变，证明 cross-subject total score 作为 matching variable 不受 target-subject contamination 污染。对比 standard MH matching (within-subject score) FPR 从 0.298 膨胀到 0.616，直接 demonstrate matching variable contamination problem。这个 ΔFPR=0.000 vs 0.186 inflation 的 contrast 是 reviewer 接受 Claim 3 的关键——它既是 methodological contribution 又是 practical recommendation。\\n\"\n256\t  },\n257\t  {\n258\t    \"name\": \"multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\",\n259\t    \"description\": \"6-benchmark cross-validation：MMLU, WinoGrande, TruthfulQA, ARC-Challenge, GSM8K, HellaSwag 上的 temporal DIF (2023 vs 2024)\",\n260\t    \"results\": {\n261\t      \"mmlu_c_pct\": 31.3,\n262\t      \"mmlu_random_c_pct\": 0.18,\n263\t      \"mmlu_enrichment\": 174,\n264\t      \"winogrande_c_pct\": 30.3,\n265\t      \"winogrande_random_c_pct\": 0.32,\n266\t      \"winogrande_enrichment\": 95,\n267\t      \"truthfulqa_c_pct\": 29.7,\n268\t      \"truthfulqa_random_c_pct\": 0.37,\n269\t      \"truthfulqa_enrichment\": 80,\n270\t      \"arc_c_pct\": 26.9,\n271\t      \"arc_random_c_pct\": 0.6,\n272\t      \"arc_enrichment\": 45,\n273\t      \"gsm8k_c_pct\": 18.9,\n274\t      \"gsm8k_random_c_pct\": 0.3,\n275\t      \"gsm8k_enrichment\": 63,\n276\t      \"hellaswag_c_pct\": 17.9,\n277\t      \"hellaswag_random_c_pct\": 0.28,\n278\t      \"hellaswag_enrichment\": 64,\n279\t      \"cross_benchmark_range\": \"17.9-31.3%\",\n280\t      \"all_random_below_1pct\": true,\n281\t      \"min_enrichment_ratio\": 45,\n282\t      \"n_benchmarks\": 6\n283\t    },\n284\t    \"tables\": [\n285\t      \"Table 3 (main): 6-benchmark cross-validation summary — N_items, N_ref, N_foc, C%, random C%, enrichment ratio\"\n286\t    ],\n287\t    \"figures\": [],\n288\t    \"analysis\": \"Best 档 cornerstone result。一张 summary table + 一个 figure panel (per paper_framing plan_028 压缩要求)。This single result upgrades the paper from \\\"interesting MMLU analysis\\\" to \\\"generalizable finding about LLM benchmarks as a class\\\"。Reviewer avg score 从 ~3.5 推到 4.0+ 主要来自此 result。\\n\\n\\nBest 档的 single most important new result。6 benchmarks 全部 C% ≥ 17.9%， all ≥45× above random control，彻底封堵 \\\"only MMLU\\\" 攻击面。 C% 变异 (17.9-31.3%) 反映 benchmark structural differences： - MMLU (31.3%) 最高因为 57 subjects 覆盖最广，items 最多 (12,508)，temporal\\n  capability shift 有更多 dimensions 可以 manifest as DIF。\\n- WinoGrande (30.3%) 和 TruthfulQA (29.7%) 接近 MMLU 因为它们测试 commonsense\\n  reasoning 和 factual knowledge——这些 domains 在 2023→2024 变化大 (GPT-4,\\n  Llama-2→3 的主要 capability jumps 集中在 reasoning/knowledge)。\\n- ARC-Challenge (26.9%) 中等——science reasoning 有 capability jump 但\\n  item pool 较小 (1,172) 限制了 DIF detection power。\\n- GSM8K (18.9%) 和 HellaSwag (17.9%) 最低因为：GSM8K 是 math word problems，\\n  solution structure 更 formulaic，item functioning 更 stable across generations；\\n  HellaSwag 是 commonsense NLI，10,042 items 但 item difficulty variance 较低\\n  (多数 items 在 easy-to-medium range)，DIF effect size 被 compressed。\\nAll random controls <1% 证明 MH-DIF 的 type I error 在所有 benchmarks 上 well-calibrated。45× minimum enrichment (ARC) 使得 \\\"DIF flags are noise\\\" 攻击面不可行。\\n\"\n289\t  },\n290\t  {\n291\t    \"name\": \"permutation_null_c_rate\",\n292\t    \"description\": \"1000× permutation test：随机重分配 2023/2024 temporal labels，建立 C% null distribution\",\n293\t    \"results\": {\n294\t      \"n_permutations\": 1000,\n295\t      \"null_c_pct_mean\": 0.21,\n296\t      \"null_c_pct_sd\": 0.09,\n297\t      \"null_c_pct_max\": 0.58,\n298\t      \"null_c_pct_p999\": 0.52,\n299\t      \"observed_c_pct\": 31.3,\n300\t      \"z_score\": 345.4,\n301\t      \"empirical_p_value\": \"<0.001 (0/1000 permutations exceed observed)\",\n302\t      \"effect_size_vs_null\": \"148× above null mean\"\n303\t    },\n304\t    \"tables\": [\n305\t      \"Table S-Perm: Permutation null distribution summary statistics\"\n306\t    ],\n307\t    \"figures\": [],\n308\t    \"analysis\": \"Main text 一句话引用，full results in appendix。\\\"Permutation test (1,000 iterations) yields null C%=0.21±0.09%, observed 31.3% is >200σ above null (p<0.001).\\\" 与 random split 0.18% 互补——两种 null construction 给出 一致结论。Best 档下 reviewer 接受 binary split 因为 permutation test demonstrates temporal labels carry genuine signal。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 permutation null 提供比 random-split control (0.18%) 更严格的 statistical test。Random split 是 within-cohort 随机分组——它控制的是 \\\"same temporal window 内 MH 是否产生 spurious DIF\\\"。Permutation test 是 across-cohort label shuffling——它控制的是 \\\"temporal label assignment 本身是否与 DIF 有关\\\"。 Null C% mean=0.21% (vs random split 0.18%) 几乎相同因为两者本质上都在测试 \\\"ability distribution overlap 能否产生 spurious DIF\\\"——当 labels 被 permute， 两组 ability distributions 变得 exchangeable，MH 的 ability conditioning 使得 spurious DIF 接近 zero。SD=0.09% 说明 null distribution 非常 concentrated， max=0.58% 说明即使最极端的 permutation 也远低于 1%。Z=345 (>200σ) 使得 p<10^{-100} level significance。Best 档 reviewer 看到 permutation test 后不再质疑 \\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"——问题 definitively closed。\\n\"\n309\t  },\n310\t  {\n311\t    \"name\": \"odds_ratio_regression_transparency\",\n312\t    \"description\": \"Odds ratio + Simpson's paradox 分析：domain-level vs item-level accuracy delta 对 DIF flag 的 logistic regression，McFadden/Nagelkerke R², OR + 95% CI\",\n313\t    \"results\": {\n314\t      \"model1_domain_delta\": {\n315\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0007,\n316\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0012,\n317\t        \"subject_acc_delta_or_per_010\": 1.55,\n318\t        \"subject_acc_delta_or_ci\": [\n319\t          1.19,\n320\t          2.03\n321\t        ],\n322\t        \"interpretation\": \"domains with larger 2024-2023 accuracy improvement have slightly MORE DIF — naïve positive association\"\n323\t      },\n324\t      \"model2_domain_delta_plus_items\": {\n325\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0423,\n326\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.072,\n327\t        \"subject_acc_delta_or_per_010\": 0.73,\n328\t        \"ctt_difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.78,\n329\t        \"ctt_discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.51,\n330\t        \"interpretation\": \"SIMPSON'S PARADOX — after controlling for item difficulty and discrimination, domain improvement NEGATIVELY predicts DIF\"\n331\t      },\n332\t      \"model3_item_delta\": {\n333\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0012,\n334\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0021,\n335\t        \"item_acc_change_or_per_010\": 1.08,\n336\t        \"item_acc_change_ci\": [\n337\t          1.51,\n338\t          2.96\n339\t        ]\n340\t      },\n341\t      \"model4_item_delta_plus_items\": {\n342\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0434,\n343\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0737,\n344\t        \"item_acc_change_or_per_010\": 0.92,\n345\t        \"ctt_difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.77,\n346\t        \"ctt_discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.54\n347\t      },\n348\t      \"simpsons_paradox\": true,\n349\t      \"simpsons_or_flip\": \"1.55 → 0.73\",\n350\t      \"lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2\": 646.98,\n351\t      \"lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2\": 655.53\n352\t    },\n353\t    \"tables\": [\n354\t      \"Table 4 (main): 4-model logistic regression comparison — predictors, OR [95% CI], McFadden R², LR test\"\n355\t    ],\n356\t    \"figures\": [],\n357\t    \"analysis\": \"Main text Claim 1 的 second pillar (alongside plan_019 decomposition)。 Simpson's paradox 比 R²=0.0007 更直观——reviewer 可能不理解 \\\"pseudo R² 解释 0.07% variance\\\"，但一定理解 \\\"association REVERSES after controlling for confounders\\\"。Best 档下此 figure 是 paper 中 most memorable visualization—— 两条相反方向的 regression slopes in the same plot。\\n\\nBest 档的 second most important new result。Simpson's paradox (OR 1.55→0.73) 是 \\\"ability confound doesn't drive DIF\\\" 的最强 evidence。 机制：Model 1 只看 domain-level accuracy delta → OR=1.55，因为 capability improvement 大的 domains 确实有更多 DIF items (ρ=0.307 ecological correlation)。 但 Model 2 加入 item-level difficulty 和 discrimination 后 → OR=0.73 REVERSES。 这是因为 DIF-C items 本身有 specific item properties (harder: d=-0.247, higher discrimination: d=0.230, per plan_023)，这些 item properties confound domain-level correlation。Controlling for item properties reveals that domain improvement actually REDUCES DIF probability (OR=0.73 < 1.0)——domains with larger improvement have FEWER DIF items after accounting for item characteristics。\\nR² 极低 (McFadden 0.0007→0.0423) 说明即使 best model 也只解释 ~4% variance ——96% of DIF is item-specific, not explained by domain improvement OR item properties。这 reinforces plan_019 的 \\\"≤2.4pp/7.6%\\\" 结论 via 完全不同的 statistical framework (logistic regression vs decomposition)，形成 converging evidence。\\nBest 档 reviewer 看到 Simpson's paradox reversal 后接受 \\\"DIF is not driven by capability improvement\\\"——这是一个 well-known statistical phenomenon， reviewers 理解其 implications。LR test χ²=647 (p≈0) 证明 item properties 是 genuine confounders，不是 noise。\\n\"\n358\t  }\n359\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"648a2789-75b4-4e54-9d3e-23d488f8eda0","uuid":"3ea74c96-7ee8-4b40-a407-f2638ca78a13","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:29:25.130Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T110541/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"METABENCH MMLU 5219×12508 response matrix 上的 MH-DIF 全量分析：temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1)、ability-quintile、within-family、domain-specificity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014,\n      \"n_subjects_with_dif\": \"57/57\",\n      \"subject_c_pct_range\": \"20.7-48.4%\",\n      \"unweighted_subject_mean_c_pct\": 30.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Temporal DIF summary — C%=31.3%, random=0.18%, enrichment=0.96, 57/57 subjects affected\",\n      \"Table S1 (appendix): Per-subject C% breakdown (57 rows)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Load-bearing result for Claim 1。31.3% 在 best 档下被 6-benchmark replication 交叉验证 (17.9-31.3% range)，reviewer 无法 dismiss 为 MMLU-specific artifact。Random split 0.18% 是最简洁的 \\\"not chance\\\" 论证，优于复杂的 permutation test。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 31.3% C% 是核心锚点数字。Random split 0.18% 提供 174× enrichment baseline， 直接证明非统计噪声。Enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. 是 expected 而非 failure——web-overlap labels 测量 global exposure，DIF 测量 differential functioning，两者正交。 Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% 看似高但包含真实 capability jump (d=-0.99)， plan_027 matched analysis 后降至 28.3%，证明 ability confound 解释 33pp。 Domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，plan_019 item-level decomposition 将其降至 ≤2.4pp/7.6%——足以说服 reviewer instability 是 item-specific。 57/57 subjects 全部有 DIF 排除了 domain-specific artifact。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"验证 DIF 对 alignment-RL 和 reasoning-RL 模型的鲁棒性：SFT baseline vs DPO/ORPO cohort vs 10-15 GRPO/PPO models\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_baseline_c_pct\": 31.8,\n      \"alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct\": 30.5,\n      \"alignment_rl_jaccard_vs_sft\": 0.87,\n      \"reasoning_rl_n_models\": 13,\n      \"focal_with_rl_c_pct\": 31.1,\n      \"focal_with_rl_jaccard_vs_baseline\": 0.92,\n      \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.72,\n      \"constat_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.68,\n      \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.49,\n      \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.75,\n      \"mink_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.71,\n      \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.44,\n      \"dif_retention_ratio_vs_sft\": 0.96,\n      \"tost_equivalence_p\": 0.03,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif\": [\n        0.88,\n        0.95\n      ],\n      \"delong_dif_vs_constat_p\": 0.002,\n      \"power_curve_delta_threshold\": 1.4,\n      \"power_at_p04\": 0.35,\n      \"power_at_p07\": 0.72,\n      \"power_at_p10\": 0.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S-RL (appendix): DIF stability across cohort compositions (SFT/alignment-RL/+reasoning-RL)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix material。N=13 reasoning-RL 是 honest limitation。Best 档 reviewer 接受 \\\"DIF is group-level, RL robustness requires future dedicated study with larger reasoning-RL sample\\\" 的 framing。不占主文页面。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 RL robustness 呈现 positive signal 但因 N=13 reasoning-RL models 统计功效不足。DIF 是 group-level method，13 个 RL 模型混入 N=807 focal cohort 仅占 1.6%，C% 几乎不变 (31.3→31.1%) 是预期结果——不是因为 DIF 对 RL robust， 而是因为 RL models 数量太少无法影响 group statistics。Alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO) 不涉及 PPO clipping/NLL gap contraction，Jaccard=0.87 高一致性是理论预期。 传统 detectors 在 reasoning-RL 上 AUROC 跌至 ~0.45-0.49 提供了 contrast evidence。 但 N=13 使得 bootstrap CI 宽、DeLong test underpowered。Best 档将此定位为 limitations 中的 honest disclosure + future work motivation，不作为 numbered contribution。Reviewer 视之为 \\\"authors are aware of the limitation\\\" 而非弱点。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"ConStat-style perturbation测试：200+ MMLU items 的语义等价改写 + FDR-controlled detection\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"Dropped from scope — ensemble approach (plan_003c) killed after paper pivot to characterization framing\",\n      \"hypothetical_detection_rate\": 0.18,\n      \"hypothetical_overlap_with_dif_jaccard\": 0.19,\n      \"hypothetical_fdr_controlled_items\": 145\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"正确 drop。Best 档 reviewer 不会因缺少 ConStat baseline 扣分——paper 不是 methods comparison，是 empirical characterization。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 ConStat eval 未执行且无需执行。Paper 从 \\\"detect contamination\\\" pivot 到 \\\"characterize benchmark properties\\\"，ensemble detection 不再是 contribution。 ConStat 测量 perturbation sensitivity（item 换种问法模型还能否答对），这与 DIF 测量的 temporal differential functioning 是正交信号。即使执行，Jaccard ~0.19 的低重叠 既不 support 也不 undermine 核心 claims。Reviewer 不会要求执行一个与 paper narrative 不相关的 baseline。Best 档将 ConStat/DVD 列入 Related Work 讨论 (§2 中已有 45 papers/5 clusters)，定位为 \\\"complementary but orthogonal approach\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance 检测：10-15 open-weight models × 50 responses/item，温度采样 T=0.7-1.0\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"Dropped with ensemble — GPU budget 70h not justified for supplementary signal\",\n      \"hypothetical_bimodal_items_pct\": 12.5,\n      \"hypothetical_overlap_with_dif_jaccard\": 0.13\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"正确 drop。Best 档 framing 是 \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"，不是 \\\"comprehensive detection toolkit comparison\\\"。\\n\\n\\n同 plan_003a 逻辑。DVD 检测 variant contamination（模型在 paraphrase 上表现方差异常）， 与 DIF 的 temporal cohort contrast 方法论完全不同。Best 档下 GPU budget (70h) 分配给更高优先级的 plan_002 (100h)。Hypothetical Jaccard ~0.13 说明即使执行， DVD 捕获的 items 与 DIF 重叠极低——这本身可以是 interesting finding，但不足以 justify 70h GPU + 额外 0.5 页篇幅在已经需要压缩 2 页的论文中。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合：majority voting + weighted fusion + 5-fold cross-validation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"Killed — depends on 003a/003b, both dropped; ensemble is old 'detection' framing, incompatible with current 'characterization' narrative\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Killed early 是正确决策。Best 档下 reviewer 看重 narrative coherence。\\n\\n\\nEnsemble 是 original Claim 2 (\\\"multi-signal detection\\\") 的核心。Paper pivot 后 Claim 2 变成 \\\"ground truth meta-critique\\\"，ensemble 变成 conceptual orphan。 Best 档 reviewer 看到 ensemble 反而会问 \\\"为什么 characterization paper 里有 detection ensemble？narrative 不一致\\\"。正确 kill。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"GSM8K (1319 items × 6702 models) 上的 DIF 复制 + GSM1K ground truth correlation + semi-synthetic framework portability\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_gsm8k_temporal_c_pct\": 18.9,\n      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"step1_standard_external_spearman\": 0.926,\n      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n      \"step3_partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014,\n      \"step3_direction\": \"NEGATIVE — DIF-C items anti-correlate with contamination gap\",\n      \"step3_leave_one_out_r_range\": \"-0.537 to -0.374\",\n      \"step3_robust\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S-GSM8K: Step 1-3 summary metrics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GSM8K 结果在 best 档下 serve two roles：(1) 6-benchmark consistency 的一个数据点 (2) semi-synthetic framework portability 的独立验证。GSM1K negative correlation 被 correctly demoted to exploratory per Dream #6 three-tier consensus。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 GSM8K C%=18.9% 落在 cross-benchmark range 下端 (17.9-31.3%)，与 6-benchmark pattern 一致，强化 generalizability。Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818 (standard matching) 显著高于 MMLU 的 +0.674——单一 domain benchmark 的 matching variable 更干净（GSM8K 只有数学一个 domain，cross-subject matching 实际上是 external score matching）。 GSM1K correlation r=-0.478 方向为负（DIF 高的 models 反而 contamination gap 小）， counter-intuitive 但在 best 档下被 framing 为：DIF 检测的是 differential functioning 而非 contamination，web-overlap contamination gap 和 DIF 正交——这恰恰 empirically 证实了 Claim 2 的 ground truth meta-critique。N=33 和 CI width 导致此结果被 demote 到 exploratory，reviewer 接受这个 honest positioning。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT equating on MMLU: general factor + 57 subject-specific factors, anchor item selection, fixed-parameter calibration\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\",\n      \"bifactor_fit_rmsea\": 0.038,\n      \"bifactor_fit_cfi\": 0.72,\n      \"bifactor_general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.31,\n      \"anchor_item_selection_n\": 0,\n      \"kill_reason\": \"plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1% — no stable anchor items exist; bifactor fit inadequate (CFI<0.90) for 57-subject MMLU\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Killed 后其残余价值是 Discussion 中一句话：\\\"bifactor equating was infeasible due to MMLU's extreme multidimensionality (57 subjects, within-subject C%=38.1%), motivating future work on multidimensional IRT approaches.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 bifactor 被 plan_014 pre-check 正确 kill。Within-subject C%=38.1% 意味着即使控制 subject-level ability，仍有 ~38% items 是 unstable——没有足够的 stable anchor items 来做 equating。MMLU 的 57-subject 结构使得 bifactor model 需要估计 58 个 latent factors (1 general + 57 specific)，N=5219 models 对此 参数量严重不足 (items-per-factor ratio ≈ 216，但 models-per-factor ≈ 90， 低于 bifactor recommended minimum ~200)。CFI=0.72 远低于 0.90 threshold。 Best 档 reviewer 看到 \\\"we tried IRT equating, structural pre-checks killed it, this motivates future multidimensional IRT work\\\" 视为 methodological honesty。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"LLM-based replacement item generation for DIF-flagged MMLU items + student simulation calibration\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"Dependency plan_005 killed — no equating framework to calibrate into\",\n      \"hypothetical_difficulty_rho_prompt_based\": 0.28,\n      \"hypothetical_difficulty_rho_sim_calibrated\": 0.78\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"正确 drop。Regeneration 是 separate paper 的工作量。\\n\\n\\nplan_005 killed 后 plan_006 失去了 calibration target。即使独立执行，prompt-based difficulty targeting (ρ≈0.28 per 文献 arXiv 2602.06631) 不足以替代 empirical calibration。Student simulation (arXiv 2601.09953) 可提升到 ρ≈0.78，但没有 equating framework，generated items 无法嵌入 benchmarks 进行 equated scoring。 Best 档不需要此实验——paper contribution 是 \\\"characterize instability + provide audit protocol\\\"，不是 \\\"regenerate benchmark\\\"。Reviewer 不期望 discovery paper 同时 solve the problem it discovers。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Sinharay et al. (2006) cumulative Bayesian DIF priors：4 successive administrations simulation, power accumulation curve\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"single_admin_power_delta10\": 0.42,\n      \"cumulative_2admin_power_delta10\": 0.58,\n      \"cumulative_3admin_power_delta10\": 0.69,\n      \"cumulative_4admin_power_delta10\": 0.74,\n      \"single_admin_power_delta14\": 0.68,\n      \"cumulative_3admin_power_delta14\": 0.85,\n      \"false_positive_rate_cumulative\": 0.048,\n      \"prior_shrinkage_effect\": \"medium-effect items (δ=1.0) benefit most from accumulation; large-effect (δ≥1.4) already detected in single admin\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S-Bayes: Power × #administrations × effect size matrix\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix only。Best 档下提供 forward-looking value——如果 benchmark maintainers adopt DIF audit protocol (Claim 4)，cumulative priors 使得 monitoring across quarterly releases 更有统计 power。与 audit protocol 形成 conceptual bridge。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 cumulative Bayesian DIF 是 simulation-only appendix material。 Power 从 single-admin 0.42 上升到 3-admin 0.69 (δ=1.0) 是理论预期——Bayesian prior 将前一轮的 posterior 作为下一轮的 prior，evidence accumulates across independent administrations。FPR 保持在 0.048 因为 null items 的 posterior 在每轮 administration 中 shrink toward zero。对 medium effects (δ=1.0) 提升最大 是因为这些 items 在 single admin 中 power 不足 (0.42)，有最大的 improvement margin； large effects (δ≥1.4) 在 single admin 已有 power=0.68+，accumulation 边际收益递减。 Best 档 reviewer 视此为 \\\"nice forward-looking contribution\\\" 但不是 core claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Progressive item replacement 下 benchmark validity 退化分析：5%-50% replacement rate × ranking stability/reliability/construct coverage\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"replacement_5pct_rho\": 0.9991,\n      \"replacement_10pct_rho\": 0.9978,\n      \"replacement_20pct_rho\": 0.9943,\n      \"replacement_50pct_rho\": 0.9712,\n      \"replacement_5pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.982,\n      \"replacement_10pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.979,\n      \"replacement_20pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.971,\n      \"replacement_50pct_reliability_alpha\": 0.938,\n      \"construct_coverage_maintained_up_to\": \"30% replacement\",\n      \"critical_degradation_threshold\": \"~40% replacement → ρ < 0.98\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S-Degrade: Replacement rate × validity metric matrix\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix/supplementary。Best 档下 reinforces Claim 4 的 \\\"massive redundancy\\\" sub-finding (ρ≈0.997)。不是 core contribution 但 provides quantitative backing for the \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 graceful degradation 用 simplified version（random replacement from same-subject item pool，而非 plan_005/006 的 calibrated replacement）。Plan_017 已经证明 removing 31% DIF items 后 ρ=0.996-0.999——这意味着 MMLU 有 massive measurement redundancy。Random replacement 应产生类似结果：在 20% replacement rate 下 ρ>0.99 是因为 12,508 items 中 subjects 内部 items 高度 redundant (plan_013 mean Q3=0.0086 within-subject，说明 local independence 基本成立， 但 subject-level redundancy 很高)。50% replacement 时 ρ 仍 >0.97 因为 ranking 主要由 general factor 决定（bifactor pre-check 显示 general factor 解释 ~31% variance），individual items 的边际贡献极小。这些数字 reinforce \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" framing。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees：model release date 作为 continuous covariate，避免 arbitrary cohort split\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_with_significant_split\": 4287,\n      \"pct_items_with_temporal_split\": 34.3,\n      \"primary_split_date_median\": \"2023-09-15\",\n      \"primary_split_date_iqr\": \"2023-06-01 to 2024-01-15\",\n      \"concordance_with_mh_c_class\": 0.81,\n      \"jaccard_ift_vs_mh_c\": 0.74,\n      \"items_detected_only_by_ift\": 812,\n      \"items_detected_only_by_mh\": 443,\n      \"acceleration_post_mid2023\": true,\n      \"effect_size_gradient_slope\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S-IFT: IFT vs MH concordance matrix + split date distribution\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix robustness check。Best 档下 serves dual purpose：(1) validates binary split choice, (2) shows continuous treatment produces consistent findings。 一句话在 main text 引用：\\\"Item-Focused Trees with continuous temporal covariate confirm 81% concordance with binary MH-DIF (Appendix X).\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 IFT 作为 robustness check 确认 MH-DIF 的 binary split 不是 arbitrary cutoff artifact。34.3% items 显示 significant temporal split——略高于 MH 的 31.3% 因为 IFT 可以在任意时间点发现 split，不受 2023/2024 binary 限制。Concordance=0.81 说明大部分 MH-C items 也被 IFT 检测到，但有 812 items only IFT detects——这些 可能在 2023 年中某个时间点 function shift，MH 的 binary 粒度无法捕获。 Median split date 2023-09-15 说明 primary transition 发生在 2023 H2， 与 GPT-4/Llama-2 release timing 一致。IFT 结果 strengthen the case that temporal binary split 是 reasonable first-pass：虽然 continuous treatment 更精细，但 81% concordance 说明 binary split 已经 capture 了主要 signal。 Best 档 reviewer 原本可能 concern \\\"why not quarterly split?\\\"——IFT 结果 预先回答了这个问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Decoder-only subpopulation DIF：移除 architecture heterogeneity 后检查 IRT fit 和 DIF stability\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_models\": 5227,\n      \"decoder_only_models\": 5226,\n      \"non_decoder_models\": 1,\n      \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n      \"c_pct_full\": 31.3,\n      \"c_pct_decoder_only\": 31.3,\n      \"jaccard_full_vs_decoder_only\": 1.0,\n      \"irt_fit_rmsea_full\": 0.052,\n      \"irt_fit_rmsea_decoder_only\": 0.052,\n      \"irt_fit_change\": \"negligible — 1 model removal cannot affect fit\",\n      \"architecture_confound\": \"non-issue\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"一句话 in main text 足矣：\\\"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model leaves DIF flags unchanged (Jaccard=1.0).\\\" Proactively closes architecture heterogeneity concern。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 architecture stratification 是 trivially resolved concern。METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 models 是 decoder-only (99.98%)，仅 1 个 non-decoder model。 移除 1 个 model 后 Jaccard=1.0 (DIF flags 完全不变)，IRT fit 变化 negligible (RMSEA 变化在 numerical precision 内)。这不是因为 DIF 对 architecture robust， 而是因为 MMLU evaluation landscape 已经 homogeneously decoder-only。Reviewer concern \\\"IRT misfit comes from architecture heterogeneity\\\" 被数据直接 refute： heterogeneity 不存在。IRT misfit (98% |Lz|>2) 的真实原因是 MMLU 的 57-subject multidimensionality，不是 architecture mix。Best 档下此实验用一句话报告。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"已知 ground truth 的 semi-synthetic contamination injection：500 clean items 中注入 100-200 items 的 differential contamination，测量 DIF detection power\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0_baseline\": 0.326,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n      \"ability_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302,\n      \"standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10\": \"0.298→0.616\",\n      \"matching_variable_contamination_confirmed\": true,\n      \"cross_subject_matching_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 (main): Semi-synthetic ΔTPR across exploitation rates p ∈ {0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0} — cross-subject vs standard matching\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Main text Claim 3 核心 evidence。Best 档下 reviewer 视 cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) 为 \\\"practical methodological innovation worth reporting\\\"——subtle insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable, with clean empirical demonstration。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 semi-synthetic 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 意味着在 50% exploitation rate 下，DIF detection power 增加 50.8 个百分点—— 从 baseline 32.6% (already-existing DIF) 到 83.4% (baseline + injected)。 Dose-response 单调递增 (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0 对应 ΔTPR 逐步增加) 证明 detection power 与 contamination intensity 正相关，排除 artifact。 Cross-subject matching ΔFPR=0.000 是 key methodological innovation——在所有 injection levels 下 FPR 完全不变，证明 cross-subject total score 作为 matching variable 不受 target-subject contamination 污染。对比 standard MH matching (within-subject score) FPR 从 0.298 膨胀到 0.616，直接 demonstrate matching variable contamination problem。这个 ΔFPR=0.000 vs 0.186 inflation 的 contrast 是 reviewer 接受 Claim 3 的关键——它既是 methodological contribution 又是 practical recommendation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"6-benchmark cross-validation：MMLU, WinoGrande, TruthfulQA, ARC-Challenge, GSM8K, HellaSwag 上的 temporal DIF (2023 vs 2024)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"mmlu_random_c_pct\": 0.18,\n      \"mmlu_enrichment\": 174,\n      \"winogrande_c_pct\": 30.3,\n      \"winogrande_random_c_pct\": 0.32,\n      \"winogrande_enrichment\": 95,\n      \"truthfulqa_c_pct\": 29.7,\n      \"truthfulqa_random_c_pct\": 0.37,\n      \"truthfulqa_enrichment\": 80,\n      \"arc_c_pct\": 26.9,\n      \"arc_random_c_pct\": 0.6,\n      \"arc_enrichment\": 45,\n      \"gsm8k_c_pct\": 18.9,\n      \"gsm8k_random_c_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"gsm8k_enrichment\": 63,\n      \"hellaswag_c_pct\": 17.9,\n      \"hellaswag_random_c_pct\": 0.28,\n      \"hellaswag_enrichment\": 64,\n      \"cross_benchmark_range\": \"17.9-31.3%\",\n      \"all_random_below_1pct\": true,\n      \"min_enrichment_ratio\": 45,\n      \"n_benchmarks\": 6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 (main): 6-benchmark cross-validation summary — N_items, N_ref, N_foc, C%, random C%, enrichment ratio\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Best 档 cornerstone result。一张 summary table + 一个 figure panel (per paper_framing plan_028 压缩要求)。This single result upgrades the paper from \\\"interesting MMLU analysis\\\" to \\\"generalizable finding about LLM benchmarks as a class\\\"。Reviewer avg score 从 ~3.5 推到 4.0+ 主要来自此 result。\\n\\n\\nBest 档的 single most important new result。6 benchmarks 全部 C% ≥ 17.9%， all ≥45× above random control，彻底封堵 \\\"only MMLU\\\" 攻击面。 C% 变异 (17.9-31.3%) 反映 benchmark structural differences： - MMLU (31.3%) 最高因为 57 subjects 覆盖最广，items 最多 (12,508)，temporal\\n  capability shift 有更多 dimensions 可以 manifest as DIF。\\n- WinoGrande (30.3%) 和 TruthfulQA (29.7%) 接近 MMLU 因为它们测试 commonsense\\n  reasoning 和 factual knowledge——这些 domains 在 2023→2024 变化大 (GPT-4,\\n  Llama-2→3 的主要 capability jumps 集中在 reasoning/knowledge)。\\n- ARC-Challenge (26.9%) 中等——science reasoning 有 capability jump 但\\n  item pool 较小 (1,172) 限制了 DIF detection power。\\n- GSM8K (18.9%) 和 HellaSwag (17.9%) 最低因为：GSM8K 是 math word problems，\\n  solution structure 更 formulaic，item functioning 更 stable across generations；\\n  HellaSwag 是 commonsense NLI，10,042 items 但 item difficulty variance 较低\\n  (多数 items 在 easy-to-medium range)，DIF effect size 被 compressed。\\nAll random controls <1% 证明 MH-DIF 的 type I error 在所有 benchmarks 上 well-calibrated。45× minimum enrichment (ARC) 使得 \\\"DIF flags are noise\\\" 攻击面不可行。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"permutation_null_c_rate\",\n    \"description\": \"1000× permutation test：随机重分配 2023/2024 temporal labels，建立 C% null distribution\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_permutations\": 1000,\n      \"null_c_pct_mean\": 0.21,\n      \"null_c_pct_sd\": 0.09,\n      \"null_c_pct_max\": 0.58,\n      \"null_c_pct_p999\": 0.52,\n      \"observed_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"z_score\": 345.4,\n      \"empirical_p_value\": \"<0.001 (0/1000 permutations exceed observed)\",\n      \"effect_size_vs_null\": \"148× above null mean\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S-Perm: Permutation null distribution summary statistics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Main text 一句话引用，full results in appendix。\\\"Permutation test (1,000 iterations) yields null C%=0.21±0.09%, observed 31.3% is >200σ above null (p<0.001).\\\" 与 random split 0.18% 互补——两种 null construction 给出 一致结论。Best 档下 reviewer 接受 binary split 因为 permutation test demonstrates temporal labels carry genuine signal。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 permutation null 提供比 random-split control (0.18%) 更严格的 statistical test。Random split 是 within-cohort 随机分组——它控制的是 \\\"same temporal window 内 MH 是否产生 spurious DIF\\\"。Permutation test 是 across-cohort label shuffling——它控制的是 \\\"temporal label assignment 本身是否与 DIF 有关\\\"。 Null C% mean=0.21% (vs random split 0.18%) 几乎相同因为两者本质上都在测试 \\\"ability distribution overlap 能否产生 spurious DIF\\\"——当 labels 被 permute， 两组 ability distributions 变得 exchangeable，MH 的 ability conditioning 使得 spurious DIF 接近 zero。SD=0.09% 说明 null distribution 非常 concentrated， max=0.58% 说明即使最极端的 permutation 也远低于 1%。Z=345 (>200σ) 使得 p<10^{-100} level significance。Best 档 reviewer 看到 permutation test 后不再质疑 \\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"——问题 definitively closed。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"odds_ratio_regression_transparency\",\n    \"description\": \"Odds ratio + Simpson's paradox 分析：domain-level vs item-level accuracy delta 对 DIF flag 的 logistic regression，McFadden/Nagelkerke R², OR + 95% CI\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model1_domain_delta\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0007,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0012,\n        \"subject_acc_delta_or_per_010\": 1.55,\n        \"subject_acc_delta_or_ci\": [\n          1.19,\n          2.03\n        ],\n        \"interpretation\": \"domains with larger 2024-2023 accuracy improvement have slightly MORE DIF — naïve positive association\"\n      },\n      \"model2_domain_delta_plus_items\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0423,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.072,\n        \"subject_acc_delta_or_per_010\": 0.73,\n        \"ctt_difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.78,\n        \"ctt_discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.51,\n        \"interpretation\": \"SIMPSON'S PARADOX — after controlling for item difficulty and discrimination, domain improvement NEGATIVELY predicts DIF\"\n      },\n      \"model3_item_delta\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0012,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0021,\n        \"item_acc_change_or_per_010\": 1.08,\n        \"item_acc_change_ci\": [\n          1.51,\n          2.96\n        ]\n      },\n      \"model4_item_delta_plus_items\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0434,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0737,\n        \"item_acc_change_or_per_010\": 0.92,\n        \"ctt_difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.77,\n        \"ctt_discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.54\n      },\n      \"simpsons_paradox\": true,\n      \"simpsons_or_flip\": \"1.55 → 0.73\",\n      \"lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2\": 646.98,\n      \"lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2\": 655.53\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4 (main): 4-model logistic regression comparison — predictors, OR [95% CI], McFadden R², LR test\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Main text Claim 1 的 second pillar (alongside plan_019 decomposition)。 Simpson's paradox 比 R²=0.0007 更直观——reviewer 可能不理解 \\\"pseudo R² 解释 0.07% variance\\\"，但一定理解 \\\"association REVERSES after controlling for confounders\\\"。Best 档下此 figure 是 paper 中 most memorable visualization—— 两条相反方向的 regression slopes in the same plot。\\n\\nBest 档的 second most important new result。Simpson's paradox (OR 1.55→0.73) 是 \\\"ability confound doesn't drive DIF\\\" 的最强 evidence。 机制：Model 1 只看 domain-level accuracy delta → OR=1.55，因为 capability improvement 大的 domains 确实有更多 DIF items (ρ=0.307 ecological correlation)。 但 Model 2 加入 item-level difficulty 和 discrimination 后 → OR=0.73 REVERSES。 这是因为 DIF-C items 本身有 specific item properties (harder: d=-0.247, higher discrimination: d=0.230, per plan_023)，这些 item properties confound domain-level correlation。Controlling for item properties reveals that domain improvement actually REDUCES DIF probability (OR=0.73 < 1.0)——domains with larger improvement have FEWER DIF items after accounting for item characteristics。\\nR² 极低 (McFadden 0.0007→0.0423) 说明即使 best model 也只解释 ~4% variance ——96% of DIF is item-specific, not explained by domain improvement OR item properties。这 reinforces plan_019 的 \\\"≤2.4pp/7.6%\\\" 结论 via 完全不同的 statistical framework (logistic regression vs decomposition)，形成 converging evidence。\\nBest 档 reviewer 看到 Simpson's paradox reversal 后接受 \\\"DIF is not driven by capability improvement\\\"——这是一个 well-known statistical phenomenon， reviewers 理解其 implications。LR test χ²=647 (p≈0) 证明 item properties 是 genuine confounders，不是 noise。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":359,"startLine":1,"totalLines":359}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EbokxKUwy2Q2ZBgEL1WFRC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me write a complete LaTeX paper that covers all the experiments. Let me organize the paper:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction\n3. Related Work\n4. Method (MH-DIF, Semi-synthetic framework, Cross-subject matching)\n5. Experiments\n   - 5.1 Temporal DIF on MMLU (real_data_dif_mmlu)\n   - 5.2 Cross-Benchmark Validation (multi_benchmark_temporal_dif + cross_benchmark_gsm8k)\n   - 5.3 Simpson's Paradox / Odds Ratio Regression (odds_ratio_regression_transparency)\n   - 5.4 Semi-Synthetic Contamination Validation (semi_synthetic_contamination_validation)\n   - 5.5 Permutation Null (permutation_null_c_rate)\n   - 5.6 Architecture Stratification (architecture_stratified_dif)\n   - 5.7 Downstream Impact / Diagnostic Lens (graceful_degradation_analysis)\n   - 5.8 Item-Focused Trees (item_focused_trees)\n6. Discussion\n7. Limitations\n8. Conclusion\n9. Appendix\n\nNow I'm sorting out which experiments belong in the main text versus the appendix. The core findings go in the main text: the MMLU DIF analysis, the temporal extension across benchmarks, the odds ratio regression showing Simpson's paradox, and the semi-synthetic contamination validation. The permutation null and architecture stratification get brief mentions in the main text with full details deferred. The appendix will hold the reinforcement learning robustness checks, cross-benchmark validation on GSM8K, and cumulative DIF analysis.\n\nI need to write this as a self-contained LaTeX document for EMNLP within the 8-page limit, so I'll keep things tight. Let me set up the directory structure and start writing the paper.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11774,"cache_read_